==============================================================
 Phase 3 demo — GB-5 spend caps, GB-6 alerts, mid-stream cut
==============================================================

The 100k-token scenario, five lines of YAML (demo/budget.yaml):

        spend_caps:
          team:
            default: 100000
            overrides:
              ml-research: 200000
              free-tier: 5000

--------------------------------------------------------------
(1)(2)(3) GB-5 default cap + GB-6 alerts + GB-4 cap rejection
--------------------------------------------------------------
team=free-tier is capped at 5_000 tokens (a per-value override). We drive
repeated requests; the running tally crosses 80% and the cap, firing the
GB-6 soft and hard alerts AT the enforcement point, then the next request
is rejected at request start with the operator's GB-4 body.

  request #1 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #2 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #3 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #4 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #5 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #6 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #7 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #8 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200

The operator's GB-4 body on the rejected request (naming cap + spend):
